.TH PVT-RENDER 1 "August 2026" "Procedural Visualizer Tool 5.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pvt-render \- render Procedural Visualizer Tool projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pvt-render
.br
.B pvt-render --render
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pvt-render --load
.I FILE
.RI [ --render ]
.br
.B pvt-render --self-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pvt-render
is the command-line editor and renderer supplied with Procedural Visualizer
Tool. With no arguments it starts an interactive menu. Options are processed
from left to right, so
.B --load
must precede any project overrides.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --load " " FILE
Open a ZIP bundle, unpacked bundle directory, or legacy .pvt project.
.TP
.BR --save " " FILE
Save a versioned project bundle.
.TP
.B --render
Render a composite frame sequence.
.TP
.BR --output-dir " " PATH
Write rendered frames under PATH.
.TP
.BR --width " " N , " " --height " " N , " " --frames " " N , " " --fps " " N
Set output dimensions, sequence length, and frame rate.
.TP
.BR --backend " " cpu|cpu+gpu|gpu
Select the rendering policy.
.TP
.BR --height-map " " PNG
Embed a PNG height map and enable the generated displacement Plane. Use
.BR --height-min ,
.BR --height-max ,
.BR --height-midpoint ,
and
.B --height-pixels-per-node
to control its signed height range and mesh density.
.TP
.BR --self-test
Run the command-line library smoke test. Use this option by itself.
.TP
.BR --version
Print the program version.
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Show the complete option reference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR procedural-visualizer-tool (1)
